[gd_scene load_steps=5 format=3]

; REPAIR LANCE, in the player's hands.
;
; A PlayerMelee with one branch added — see player_repair_lance.gd. The numbers
; that make it a lance rather than a knife are here: 3.4m of reach against the
; wrench's 2.2, and sixty damage, which is the hardest single hit in the game
; outside the Recoilless. Both are the trade for having to close.
;
; THE MODEL IS TURNED TO POINT AWAY. repair_lance.tscn runs its haft along +X
; with the head toward +X, so instanced unrotated it lies flat across the screen
; like a bar held sideways — which is exactly what it did. The basis here maps
; model +X onto camera -Z so the point goes downrange, and the whole thing sits
; angled in from the bottom-right corner so the haft runs off the frame edge.
; The butt sits 6.6cm BEHIND the eye at rest and stays clipped through the full
; thrust, which is what keeps the lance anchored instead of floating mid-screen.
;
; swing_time 1.1 with impact_at 0.14: OUT IN 0.154s, then most of a
; second of recovery. swing_time is untouched so the swing rate and the window you
; are committed for are exactly as before — only the stroke moved. It read as slow
; because 0.62 of 1.1s is a 0.68s extension AND it was routed through the pose
; lerp, which chases at pose_speed and never arrives; player_repair_lance.gd now
; drives it from _extra_position(), outside the lerp, where the timing is real.
;
; IT NEVER LOWERS. lowers_when_obstructed is false: a 3.4m polearm has something
; within the obstruction probe's reach almost everywhere indoors, so it spent its
; time dropping out of frame and coming back. obstructed_position below is still
; load-bearing — equip() snaps to it, so it is the pose the lance is drawn FROM.

;
; THE HOLSTER POSE IS A PURE DROP. obstructed_rotation repeats the rest
; orientation exactly — the 107.88 of yaw and 12.69 of roll that initialize()
; reads off the Lance node below — and obstructed_position moves only in Y. So
; drawing the lance, and lowering it into a wall, slide it down and up and never
; turn it. The class default was (0.3, 270, 3) when this was authored, which
; against a rest of 107.88 is 162 degrees of yaw whipped through in four tenths
; of a second on a 3.4m polearm. That default has since been corrected to 90 — a
; much smaller 18 — but it is still a TURN, and the point here is that the lance
; does not turn at all. Authored rather than inherited for that reason, not just
; because the old default was wrong.

; IT MAKES A NOISE NOW. The scene shipped with no AudioStreamPlayer at all, so
; swing_sound, hit_sound and click_sound were every one of them null: a thrust
; that connected sounded exactly like a thrust that did not, and running out of
; charges was silent. Two of the three stab samples, so a hit reads differently
; from a whiff.

